{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Application - OAuth2 - Okta OAuth2 Admin Consent Granted",
	"Description": "An administrator granted consent on behalf of the whole org for an OAuth2 client's scopes, or a refresh token was detected being reused. Admin consent means no user ever sees a consent prompt for that client again; token reuse detection means a refresh token was presented twice, which is what happens when one has been stolen.\n\nEvent types: app.oauth2.admin.consent.grant, app.oauth2.as.token.detect_reuse, app.oauth2.token.detect_reuse\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
